Caelza M4 phase 3b: the phone-first pass.

Measured at 390 x 844 with runtime/tools/phone-shots against every route.
Most of the pass is CSS in the overlay (web/src/caelza-brand.css: 16 px page
gutters, tables that scroll inside their card, thumb-sized controls); these
hunks fix what CSS cannot: the page header's actions slot now wraps and
shrinks instead of pushing past the edge (Tools' controls did), the header's
language button keeps only its globe on a phone so the page title is not
cut to an ellipsis, the chat toolbar wraps and its model name yields, the
Runs page gets the page padding every other page has and, with SOPs and
Plugins, a header and tab title, and the mono face is no longer fetched
from a font CDN (it is vendored; the CSP refused the fetch). Applied after
the rename, the overlay and patches 0001 to 0005; regenerate with the same
`diff -u` when the upstream pin moves.

